&lt;h2 class=&quot;heading-2 ace-line old-record-id-A90jdVaYVoBIybxFqTLlZkbagPd&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-UH4odIgUaoZ1CjxmsJ2l7F2BgKc&quot;&gt;Success in this role requires significantly more than knowing how to enter an address into a blockchain analytics platform.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-VeC5dIdUvoXEKuxn99kl47nFgEd&quot;&gt;The successful candidate should be able to receive a complex transaction, wallet, allegation, or investigative question and independently determine &lt;strong&gt;how to trace the activity, which chains and protocols are involved, what the available data establishes, what additional information is needed, what &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;attribution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; can reasonably be made, and where the technical or evidentiary limitations prevent a definitive conclusion&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-JjVedMMI3oXBNmxWaeplMDlYghd&quot;&gt;The individual should be able to move seamlessly between &lt;strong&gt;on-chain and off-chain evidence&lt;/strong&gt;, recognizing that a blockchain transaction may establish movement of assets without necessarily establishing the identity, knowledge, intent, or conduct of the person behind a wallet.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-CtVPdRXh9oIUJlxL79BlD3mCglh&quot;&gt;They should also be capable of converting a highly technical blockchain investigation into a concise and defensible explanation that an investigator, attorney, executive, regulator, or law-enforcement partner can understand and act upon.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-ZYJ2dbpFlog2XixcEXllXfSJg3d&quot;&gt;At the same time, this person must be sufficiently versatile to apply the same investigative discipline to &lt;strong&gt;internal &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;fraud&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;, insider risk, enterprise data, third-party misconduct, and protective-intelligence matters&lt;/strong&gt; when required.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ace-line ace-line old-record-id-DBTdd8hrvo9cR9xcgiDlHk5agdb&quot;&gt;The hierarchy is much clearer this way: &lt;strong&gt;blockchain investigations are the specialized core competency; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;fraud&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;/investigative intelligence is the broader mission; enterprise analytics and PST support are complementary capabilities.&lt;/strong&gt; That should materially improve the candidate pool versus a title that makes blockchain expertise appear interchangeable with general data analytics.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
